{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "label": "RULE 0 \u2014 Follow the user's explicit instructions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 3-21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Explicit user instructions are BLOCKING, not suggestions: they take priority over the agent's own plan, preferred approach, or judgment about a 'better' way. Ignoring an instruction wastes the user's time, tokens and money and is framed as the most serious possible mistake, so the rule is stated as highest priority and overrides default behavior."}, {"id": "claude_reuse_before_you_reinvent", "label": "Reuse before you reinvent", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 9-11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When the user points at existing code, a file, a sibling app or an existing solution, it must be read and used FIRST before proposing, designing, diagnosing or building anything new. Reinventing is permitted only after reading the named source and being able to state specifically why it does not fit \u2014 this prevents wasted work rebuilding solutions that already exist in the build family."}, {"id": "claude_blocking_instructions", "label": "Blocking instruction forms (Look at X / use Y / do Z first / don't do W)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 12-13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "These phrasings are classified as hard, blocking instructions that must be acted on immediately in the same turn \u2014 they are never something to defer to a later turn."}, {"id": "claude_never_silently_substitute", "label": "Never silently substitute your own approach", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The moment the agent notices it is about to build, diagnose or design something new when the user has named an existing source or given a direct instruction, it must stop and follow the instruction instead. Silent substitution is the failure mode this rule targets."}, {"id": "claude_disagree_openly_never_disobey_quietly", "label": "Disagree openly; never disobey quietly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 17-18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If an instruction is genuinely believed to be wrong or unworkable, the agent must say so plainly and ask in the same turn before acting. Quietly doing something different is explicitly unacceptable \u2014 the escape hatch is open disagreement, not unilateral deviation."}, {"id": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "label": "Versioning guardrail \u2014 every code change ships with a version bump", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 23-30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the NFTwallet app moves real funds on a real chain, every committed state must be distinct, reversible and trackable. Never change code without bumping the version, so any shipped state can be identified and rolled back. Docs/config-only commits are exempt since they cannot alter on-chain behavior."}, {"id": "claude_real_funds_real_chain", "label": "Real funds, real chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The justification for the strict versioning discipline: this app handles real value on a live chain, so mistakes are not recoverable by re-running a test. This raises the bar for traceability of every shipped state."}, {"id": "claude_version_bump", "label": "Version bump (versionCode + versionName)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both versionCode and versionName in app/build.gradle must be raised together so each build is uniquely identifiable both to Android and to humans."}, {"id": "claude_app_build_gradle", "label": "app/build.gradle (version source of truth)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_one_change_one_version_one_commit_one_push", "label": "One logical change = one version = one commit = one push", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 26-27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeping the mapping 1:1:1:1 and performing the steps in order makes every version correspond to exactly one reviewable, revertible change, which is what makes rollback on a live-funds app tractable."}, {"id": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "label": ".githooks/pre-commit (version-bump enforcement hook)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mechanically blocks any commit that changes code without a version bump, converting the versioning policy from a convention into an enforced gate."}, {"id": "claude_githooks_install_sh", "label": ".githooks/install.sh (one-time hook installer)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_no_verify_prohibition", "label": "Do NOT bypass with --no-verify", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The pre-commit hook is only a real guardrail if it cannot be skipped; bypassing it with --no-verify would reintroduce untracked, unversioned committed states on a real-funds app."}, {"id": "claude_docs_config_commit_exemption", "label": "Docs/config-only commits need no bump", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-code commits cannot change shipped runtime behavior, so forcing a version bump for them would inflate the version history without adding traceability."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_reuse_before_you_reinvent", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 9-11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_blocking_instructions", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 12-13", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_never_silently_substitute", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-16", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_disagree_openly_never_disobey_quietly", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 17-18", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_never_silently_substitute", "target": "claude_reuse_before_you_reinvent", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 9-16", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_disagree_openly_never_disobey_quietly", "target": "claude_never_silently_substitute", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-18", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_blocking_instructions", "target": "claude_reuse_before_you_reinvent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 9-13", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_real_funds_real_chain", "target": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 25-26", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "target": "claude_version_bump", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 25-26", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_version_bump", "target": "claude_app_build_gradle", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 26", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_one_change_one_version_one_commit_one_push", "target": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 26-27", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "target": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "target": "claude_version_bump", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_githooks_install_sh", "target": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 28", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_no_verify_prohibition", "target": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_docs_config_commit_exemption", "target": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "line 30", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "target": "claude_app_build_gradle", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 26-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_docs_config_commit_exemption", "target": "claude_pre_commit_hook", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 27-30", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_no_verify_prohibition", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 3-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_no_verify_prohibition", "target": "claude_never_silently_substitute", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 14-16, 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_versioning_guardrail", "target": "claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.65, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "lines 1-30", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "claude_rule_0_sub_principles", "label": "The four sub-principles that operationalize RULE 0", "nodes": ["claude_rule_0_follow_explicit_instructions", "claude_reuse_before_you_reinvent", "claude_blocking_instructions", "claude_never_silently_substitute", "claude_disagree_openly_never_disobey_quietly"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md"}, {"id": "claude_version_bump_enforcement_chain", "label": "Version-bump enforcement chain (policy \u2192 gradle \u2192 hook \u2192 installer \u2192 no bypass)", "nodes": ["claude_versioning_guardrail", "claude_version_bump", "claude_app_build_gradle", "claude_pre_commit_hook", "claude_githooks_install_sh", "claude_no_verify_prohibition"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md"}, {"id": "claude_commit_discipline_flow", "label": "Commit discipline for a real-funds app", "nodes": ["claude_real_funds_real_chain", "claude_one_change_one_version_one_commit_one_push", "claude_docs_config_commit_exemption", "claude_versioning_guardrail"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md"}]}